---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Worry Or Not privacy" description="What the Worry Or Not plugin collects: nothing." noindex={true}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-12">Worry Or Not: privacy</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-p:mb-6 prose-a:text-blue-600 prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">
      <p><em>Last updated October 5, 2026.</em></p>
      <p>
        Worry Or Not is a skills-only plugin for ChatGPT and Codex. It is a set of written instructions the model follows. It runs no server of mine, holds no accounts, and has no way to send anything to me.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-12 mb-6">What I collect</h2>
      <p>Nothing. I never see your prompts, the companies you research, the reports it produces, or who you are.</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-12 mb-6">Where your data does go</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To OpenAI, as with any ChatGPT conversation, under <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI's privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li>To the public websites the model fetches while researching, including the company's own site, the Internet Archive, and public job boards. Those sites see an ordinary page request from OpenAI's infrastructure.</li>
        <li>To any research plugin you have connected yourself, such as Exa or Firecrawl, under that vendor's terms. The plugin never asks you for a key and never stores one.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-12 mb-6">Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:aaron@aaronroy.com?subject=Worry%20Or%20Not">aaron@aaronroy.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
